# cv/.gitignore
#
# The rule here: commit what the backend needs to serve and what makes a result
# reproducible; ignore what can be regenerated or re-downloaded.
#
# handoff/ is COMMITTED on purpose. It was ignored while it was an unbuilt
# output; it is now the trained artifact the API loads (model.onnx ~6 MB, plus
# class_map.json and model_card.json). A clone without it cannot scan, and the
# class map has to stay byte-identical to the .onnx it was exported with — so
# they travel together or not at all.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Training checkpoints, ~6 MB each. The served artifact is the ONNX export in
# handoff/; these only matter for resuming or re-exporting.
#   regenerate:  python scripts/train.py --stage b ...
artifacts/*.pt

# A scratch package built by make_dev_package.py with an UNTRAINED classifier.
# Predictions are noise; it exists only to exercise wiring.
dev_package/

# The image corpus — hundreds of MB to ~2 GB. Lives outside the repo;
# data/manifest.csv records exactly which image was used and under which
# licence, which is what actually makes the training run reproducible.
data/images/
incoming*/

# ImageNet initialisation weights, ~52 MB.
#   regenerate:  python scripts/fetch_weights.py
weights/

# Stray ONNX files anywhere except the handoff package. Without the negation an
# accidental export in the working tree gets committed and quietly competes with
# the real artifact.
*.onnx
!handoff/*.onnx
